                <pb facs="0922" n="822" sameAs="frus:frus1934v01/pg822"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">341.1154L58/220: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bingham</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1933-09-06T14:00:00-04:00">September 6,
                            1933—2 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>233. Referring to paragraph 5, enclosure 1, with your despatch No. 137 of August
                    4, 1933, regarding Lewis Gun claim, please obtain and transmit copies of the
                    laws and rules of Court which made possible an appeal from the decision of Judge
                    Darling to Court of Appeals and thence to the House of Lords as alleged by
                    Foreign Office.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
